## Structural Map

Key files Claude reads first:
- `controller/[Main]Controller.java` — `@RestController` HTTP entry, request parsing, validation
- `service/[Main]Service.java` — `@Service` business logic, `@Transactional` boundary
- `repository/[Main]Repository.java` — Spring Data JPA repository interface
- `domain/[Main].java` — `@Entity` definitions (or records for DTOs ≥ Java 16)
- `config/[Main]Config.java` — `@Configuration` beans (DataSource, Web, Security)

Layers and their purpose:
- `controller/` → Parse request, validate via `@Valid`, route to service (≤50 lines each)
- `service/` → Business logic, `@Transactional` on service methods (no DB calls bypass repository)
- `repository/` → Spring Data JPA repositories; no business logic
- `domain/` (or `entity/`) → `@Entity` + DTO records; no logic, no DB calls
- `config/` → Cross-cutting beans, Spring Security, datasource pool, web config
- `exception/` → Custom domain exceptions + `@RestControllerAdvice` global handler
- `src/main/resources/db/migration/` → Flyway versioned migrations (`V<ts>__<desc>.sql`)
- `src/test/java/` → JUnit 5 tests mirroring main package layout (`*Test.java`, `*IT.java`)

