## Escalation Triggers

Repo-specific high-risk patterns. Encountering any of these during a task escalates the
Change Contract `risk_level` by one tier and requires explicit user confirmation before proceeding:

- **Editing a merged Flyway V-file**: Flyway checksums in `flyway_schema_history` make this a deploy-breaker — write a new V-file instead, never edit a merged one
- **Hibernate `ddl-auto: update` or `create` in any profile**: Flyway/Liquibase owns schema, not Hibernate — escalate immediately
- **Actuator endpoint exposure**: `/actuator/env`, `/actuator/configprops`, `/actuator/heapdump` leak secrets if exposed without auth — confirm `management.endpoints.web.exposure.include` is an explicit allowlist (never `*`)
- **Spring placeholder `${VAR:?message}`**: Bash syntax, NOT Spring — Spring parses as `default="?message"` and silently boots. Use `${VAR}` (no default → fail-fast) or `${VAR:}` + `@PostConstruct` validator
- **`double` / `float` for money**: BigDecimal is mandatory for any monetary calculation in this repo
- **Shared library modification**: Changes affect ALL downstream consumers; run `/discover-impact` before modifying any shared package
